Upstream project: QEMU -- https://www.qemu.org/
Source:           https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/qemu.git
Patched tag:      v11.1.1 (QEMU_TAG in scripts/build-qemu.sh)

0001-ui-add-alcove-display-backend.patch adds one new QEMU source file,
ui/alcove.c, and modifies five existing QEMU files: meson.build,
meson_options.txt, qapi/ui.json, qemu-options.hx and ui/meson.build.

0002-hw-nvme-reset-the-controller-before-loading-its-state.patch modifies one
existing QEMU file, hw/nvme/ctrl.c, whose header reads "This code is licensed
under the GNU GPL v2 or later."

The new file carries "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later" in its own
header (0001-ui-add-alcove-display-backend.patch line 136), with the copyright
line "Copyright (c) 2026 Alcove contributors" (line 134).

None of the five files modified by 0001 carries any per-file licensing header
(verified against the v11.1.1 tree). QEMU's own LICENSE, clause 2, covers that
case: "Source files with no licensing information are released under the GNU
General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any later version."
The modifications therefore inherit GPL-2.0-or-later as well, which is why the
identifier above applies to the whole series.

GPL-2.0-only in practice. Clause 1 of QEMU's LICENSE says "The QEMU emulator
as a whole is released under the GNU General Public License, version 2", and
its COPYING is the GNU GPL version 2, June 1991. Once this series is applied,
the source tree and any qemu-system-aarch64 binary built from it are that
whole: distributable under GPL-2.0-only. "or later" is the option this patch
grants downstream, not a claim that the combined work is anything other than
GPL-2.0.

Anyone distributing a QEMU binary built with this patch takes on the GPL's
obligations for it, including offering the corresponding source: the pinned
upstream tag plus this directory.

The MIT licence at the repository root does not apply to this directory.
